### Notes (why no scores)

- Meituan published no benchmarks for this preview; BenchmarkList records **0 benchmark rows** and states explicitly: "Meituan published no benchmarks for this preview, so its claims rest on positioning... No independent evaluation had been confirmed when it was imported." (https://benchmarklist.com/models/meituan-longcat-2.5-preview/)
- LLMperks: "This model is not on the Artificial Analysis leaderboard yet." (https://www.llmperks.com/longcat/longcat-2-5-preview)
- The only public qualitative coverage is a hands-on write-up (aichina.news, 2026-10-08) that plugged the preview into Claude Code for three coding tasks and concluded "usable, cheap enough, but not yet fast enough" — no measured benchmark numbers. LongCat's own change log lists capabilities only (multimodal understanding, coding, Claude Code compatibility), no figures. (https://longcat.chat/platform/docs/ChangeLog.html)
- LongCat 2.0 (the open-weight predecessor, a separate tracked folder) does have vendor benchmarks (SWE-bench Pro 59.5, Terminal-Bench 2.1 70.8) — but those belong to `model/longcat-2.0/` and must not be silently merged into this preview's scores.
- OpenCode usage telemetry (8.4T tokens, #8 by tokens, 252K users over 2 months) is adoption data, not a benchmark, and is not scored.

No normalized 1–100 scores are assigned; the model is treated as unmeasured.

